+# Implementer Brief 11: Dog Identity Semantics, Mount Hydration & Behavioral Test Coverage
+
+## Required Changes
+
+### 1. `virtual_dog_walker/src/ui/home_feeding.js`
+1. In `onFeedClick()`:
+   Retrieve the dog name and id from `HomeSanctuary`:
+   ```javascript
+   function onFeedClick() {
+     if (feeding) return;
+     var dogSlot = null;
+     if (window.HomeSanctuary && typeof window.HomeSanctuary.getDogSlot === 'function') {
+       try { dogSlot = window.HomeSanctuary.getDogSlot(); } catch (e) {}
+     }
+     var dog = null;
+     if (window.HomeSanctuary && typeof window.HomeSanctuary.getCompanionDog === 'function') {
+       try { dog = window.HomeSanctuary.getCompanionDog(); } catch (e) {}
+     }
+     var name = (dogSlot && dogSlot.name) || (dog && dog.name) || 'Ziggy';
+     var id = (dogSlot && (dogSlot.id || dogSlot.dogId)) || (dog && dog.id) || 'dog-1';
+     runFeed({ dogName: name, dogId: id });
+   }
+   ```
+2. In `runFeed(opts)`:
+   - `var dogName = opts.dogName || 'Ziggy';`
+   - `var dogId = opts.dogId || 'dog-1';`
+   - Phase 4 toast uses `dogName`: `var toast = dogName + ' loved the meal! ❤️'; emitToast(toast);`
+   - Phase 4 persistence uses `dogId`: `persistFeed(dogId);`
+3. In `mount()`:
+   Hydrate `lastFeedAt`:
+   ```javascript
+   lastFeedAt = readLastFeedAt();
+   ```
+4. Expose `runFeed` and `onFeedClick` in `__testHooks`:
+   ```javascript
+   window.HomeFeeding.__testHooks = {
+     simulateFeed: simulateFeed,
+     runFeed: runFeed,
+     onFeedClick: onFeedClick,
+     getState: function () { return state; },
+     isFeeding: function () { return feeding; },
+     getTimers: function () { return timers; }
+   };
+   ```
+
+### 2. `virtual_dog_walker/src/ui/home_sanctuary.js`
+In `__testHooks` on `HomeSanctuary`:
+Expose particle and state inspection hooks:
+```javascript
+window.HomeSanctuary.__testHooks = {
+  getParticles: function () { return particles; },
+  spawnParticles: spawnParticles,
+  getForcedState: function () { return forcedState; },
+  getPose: function () { return pose; }
+};
+```
+
+### 3. `virtual_dog_walker/test/test_home_sanctuary.py`
+Add executable behavioral tests:
+1. `test_exec_run_feed_emits_toast_and_resumes_roaming`:
+   Drive `runFeed` under mock timers / fast-forward and assert that:
+   - `window.showToast` is invoked with `"<DogName> loved the meal! ❤️"`
+   - `last_feed_at` stored in `localStorage` has `dogId: 'dog-1'` (or the specified id)
+   - after resumption delay, dog pose is `'auto'`, dog state returns to `'wander'`, and `feeding` is `false`.
+2. `test_exec_particles_spawn_during_eating`:
+   Set state to `'eating'`, run particle spawn, and assert `particles.length > 0` and includes heart / crumb.
+3. `test_exec_mount_hydrates_last_feed_at`:
+   Pre-seed `localStorage` with `virtual_dog_walker.last_feed_at`, call `mount()`, and assert `getLastFeedAt()` returns the hydrated JSON string.
+
+## Verification
+Run:
+`python3 -m unittest test/test_home_sanctuary.py`
+All tests must pass (0 failures, 0 errors).
